{"id":"kolu-watch-config","ord":"a0","title":"watch","desc":"The watcher's knobs, read live by the olai server (#421).\n\n`nag` CARRIES ITS CAP since #489 merged (master 8e2043ed, 2026-09-03): `30m/3` means every thirty minutes, three reminders after the first report, then quiet about that terminal until its state changes. A bare `30m` would repeat forever, which is what this vault ran all day and what the lane existed to end — the human's ruling, ~07:05 ET: a finite nag, three reminders, stored here. Set to `30m/3` by the orchestrator at 17:31 ET, minutes after the first uncapped reminder arrived from the newly deployed build.\n\nThe grammar is kolu's own (`parseNag`), so a bare number is refused with a sentence rather than run as milliseconds. The three values mirror the orchestrator's own Monitor (`kolu watch --held-for 60s --nag 30m/3 --heartbeat 30m`).","created":"2026-08-29T08:30:55-04:00","changed":"2026-09-03T17:30:50-04:00","custom":{"heartbeat":"30m","held-for":"60s","nag":"30m/3"}}
{"id":"kolu-watch-mutes","ord":"a1","title":"mutes","desc":"EMPTY BY DESIGN since 2026-09-01 (#450, merged 12b3b6ad). The mute list is gone: the doorbell derives what may ring from the board itself — a terminal rings only while an un-done node claims it, and its own step marks decide whether the event is a call or a note. There is nothing to mute, nothing to unmute, and no ignore flags to keep in step with anything.\n\nThe node stands empty rather than deleted because the file's own convention is read by name; if a genuine override is ever wanted, it is ruled with the human first.","created":"2026-08-29T08:31:02-04:00","changed":"2026-08-31T20:21:23-04:00"}
